## 4. PAYMENT FLOW (UPI intent + manual verification)

1. User selects team → sees exact fee.
2. `PAY ₹<amount> VIA UPI` button opens `upi://pay?pa=<UPI_ID>&pn=<RECEIVER>&am=<amount>&cu=INR` (values from config, amount always server-validated before the intent is generated).
3. A matching dynamic QR (same pa/pn/am/cu) is shown alongside.
4. Explicit, honest copy: *"Payment will be verified manually by the CyberWolf team. Clicking Pay does not automatically confirm your registration."*
5. User submits Transaction ID, UTR/Payment UID, and a screenshot (JPG/PNG/WEBP, size-capped, validated server-side by real file signature — not just extension/MIME header).
6. Registration is created with `paymentStatus = SUBMITTED`. Admin later sets `VERIFIED` or `REJECTED` (with required reason).

Registration status lifecycle: `DRAFT → SUBMITTED → PAYMENT_PENDING → PAYMENT_VERIFICATION → CONFIRMED | REJECTED | CANCELLED`.

Registration IDs: server-generated, unique, sequential — `WOLF-2026-00001`. Never trust a client-generated ID.

